---
title: Beef and Broccoli
image: https://www.saltandlavender.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/beef-and-broccoli-1.jpg
nutrition:
  calories: 343 kcal
  fat: 14 g
  saturated fat: 3 g
  carbohydrates: 26 g
  sugar: 15 g
  protein: 29 g
  fiber: 2 g
  sodium: 1239 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
servings: 4
cook time: 15 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
source: https://www.saltandlavender.com/beef-and-broccoli/
cuisine: American
course: Main Course
time required: 30 minutes
---

Trim off any fat from the @flank steak{1%pound}(can sub for skirt steak) and slice it across the grain into very thin bite-size pieces. 

Add @soy sauce{1/2%cup}, @water{1/2%cup}, @apple cider vinegar or rice vinegar{1/2%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1/2%tsp}, @brown sugar{1/4%cup}, @cornstarch{3%tbsp}, @ginger{1%tsp}(grated), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), and @crushed red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}(or more, to taste) to a bowl and whisk together thoroughly.

Add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to a large #skillet{} over high heat. Let the pan heat up for a few minutes (oil should be shimmering).

Add @broccoli florets{3-4%cups}(around one pound) and cook for ~{4-5%minutes}, stirring often. It should be tender-crisp. Transfer it to a plate.

Add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to the skillet. 

Add the flank steak in a single layer and don't touch it for ~{1%minute}. 

Flip it with cooking tongs and cook it for another ~{1%minute} or so.

> It cooks fast and will easily overcook and become tough. Leaving it a bit rare at this stage is ideal.

Add the broccoli florets back to the pan and pour in the sauce.  Stir until coated and the sauce has thickened (about ~{1-3%minutes}). 

Take the skillet off the heat and serve immediately.

> If the sauce becomes too thick, simply thin it out with a splash of water. If too thin add cornstarch.